{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_016sHu1wDZh46Gj8jpt8rxiu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Plan: Targeted Eval Dataset for Enhancement Coverage\n2\t\n3\t**Branch**: `004-targeted-eval-dataset` | **Date**: 2026-05-31 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)\n4\t**Input**: Feature specification from `specs/004-targeted-eval-dataset/spec.md`\n5\t\n6\t## Summary\n7\t\n8\tExtend `/skill:measure` to analyze the enhancement diff (the \"What Changed\" table from `/skill:enhance`), generate targeted test cases for enhanced patterns not already covered by the existing dataset, present them for interactive review, merge approved cases into `eval/cases/`, and run both baseline and enhanced evals against the combined dataset. This ensures the comparison reflects actual improvement in enhanced areas rather than only measuring pre-existing coverage.\n9\t\n10\t## Technical Context\n11\t\n12\t**Language/Version**: Bash (scripts), Markdown (SKILL.md skill definitions)\n13\t**Primary Dependencies**: agent-eval-harness plugin (`/eval-run`, `/eval-dataset`), yq (YAML parsing), skill plugin (`/skill:enhance`, `/skill:check`)\n14\t**Storage**: File-based eval case directories (`eval/cases/`)\n15\t**Testing**: Manual testing against real SKILL.md files with eval infrastructure\n16\t**Target Platform**: macOS/Linux (Claude Code environments)\n17\t**Project Type**: Claude Code plugin (skill modification + supporting logic)\n18\t**Performance Goals**: Targeted case generation adds no more than 30 seconds to the `/skill:measure` workflow (SC-003)\n19\t**Constraints**: No nested `claude -p` sessions; all invocations within current session; must not modify existing test cases (FR-007)\n20\t**Scale/Scope**: 1-2 targeted cases per enhanced pattern; bounded by `targeted_cases_per_pattern` in `eval.yaml`\n21\t\n22\t## Constitution Check\n23\t\n24\t*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*\n25\t\n26\tConstitution is a blank template. No gates to evaluate. Passes by default.\n27\t\n28\t## Project Structure\n29\t\n30\t### Documentation (this feature)\n31\t\n32\t```text\n33\tspecs/004-targeted-eval-dataset/\n34\t├── spec.md              # Feature specification\n35\t├── plan.md              # This file\n36\t├── research.md          # Phase 0: enhancement diff format, eval-dataset integration\n37\t├── data-model.md        # Phase 1: entity definitions\n38\t└── tasks.md             # Phase 2 output (created by /speckit-tasks)\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\t### Source Code (repository root)\n42\t\n43\t```text\n44\tskill/\n45\t├── skills/\n46\t│   └── measure/\n47\t│       └── SKILL.md           # MODIFIED: add targeted case generation steps\n48\t└── scripts/\n49\t    └── compare-runs.sh        # Existing (no changes needed)\n50\t\n51\teval.yaml                      # MODIFIED: add targeted_cases_per_pattern config\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\t**Structure Decision**: This feature modifies one existing file (`skill/skills/measure/SKILL.md`) and one config file (`eval.yaml`). No new files or directories are created in the source tree. The targeted case generation logic is embedded in the skill's procedure steps, not extracted into a separate script, because the generation relies on LLM capabilities (understanding which patterns were enhanced and what test inputs would exercise them).\n55\t\n56\t## Design Decisions\n57\t\n58\t### D1: Enhancement Diff Capture\n59\t\n60\tThe enhancement diff is captured by parsing the \"What Changed\" markdown table that `/skill:enhance` outputs in Step 9c. This table has the structure:\n61\t\n62\t```markdown\n63\t| Pattern Applied | What was added/changed | Why |\n64\t|----------------|----------------------|-----|\n65\t| Known Gotchas  | Added specific YAML validation pitfall | Domain has non-obvious failure modes |\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tAfter `/skill:enhance` completes (and the user applies changes), `/skill:measure` parses this table from the conversation output to extract:\n69\t- Pattern names from the \"Pattern Applied\" column\n70\t- Change descriptions from the \"What was added/changed\" column\n71\t\n72\tThis is the same approach used for detecting \"already optimal\" (reading conversation output for signals). No structured data file is needed because the table is well-formatted and parseable.\n73\t\n74\t**Edge case**: If the table is absent (user applied changes manually or output was truncated), treat as \"unknown diff\" and fall back to existing dataset only with a warning.\n75\t\n76\t### D2: Targeted Case Generation\n77\t\n78\tFor each pattern in the enhancement diff, `/skill:measure` generates targeted test cases by:\n79\t\n80\t1. Checking if an existing case in `eval/cases/` already targets this pattern (name-based matching on directory names and `annotations.yaml` content)\n81\t2. If not covered, invoking `/eval-dataset` with a hint about which pattern to target\n82\t3. Each generated case follows the existing case directory structure:\n83\t   ```\n84\t   eval/cases/case-NNN-targeted-<pattern-slug>/\n85\t   ├── input.yaml         # skill_path pointing to a synthetic SKILL.md\n86\t   ├── target-skill/\n87\t   │   └── SKILL.md       # Synthetic skill designed to exercise the pattern\n88\t   └── annotations.yaml   # Expected outcomes with targets_pattern metadata\n89\t   ```\n90\t\n91\tThe `annotations.yaml` includes a `targets_pattern` field for traceability:\n92\t```yaml\n93\tdescription: \"Tests gotcha handling added by enhancement\"\n94\ttargets_pattern: \"Known Gotchas\"\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\t### D3: Deduplication Strategy\n98\t\n99\tBefore generating a case for an enhanced pattern, check existing cases:\n100\t\n101\t1. Scan all directories in `eval/cases/` for `annotations.yaml` files\n102\t2. Check if any existing annotation has a `targets_pattern` field matching the pattern name\n103\t3. Also check if the directory name contains the pattern slug (e.g., `case-*-known-gotchas`)\n104\t4. Skip generation for patterns already covered\n105\t\n106\tThis is intentionally simple (string matching, not semantic analysis) to keep the workflow fast and deterministic.\n107\t\n108\t### D4: Interactive Review Flow\n109\t\n110\tAfter generating targeted cases (and before any eval run), `/skill:measure` presents a review prompt:\n111\t\n112\t1. Display a summary table of generated cases:\n113\t   ```\n114\t   | # | Case Directory | Targets Pattern | Input Synopsis |\n115\t   |---|----------------|----------------|----------------|\n116\t   | 1 | case-006-targeted-known-gotchas | Known Gotchas | YAML validation skill missing pitfall coverage |\n117\t   ```\n118\t\n119\t2. Prompt: \"Proceed with eval? (y/n/edit)\"\n120\t   - **y**: Continue with all generated cases\n121\t   - **n**: Abort, remove generated cases, run with original dataset only\n122\t   - **edit**: User modifies cases on disk, then confirms to continue\n123\t\n124\t3. If partial generation failure occurred, the summary includes a warning row for each failed pattern\n125\t\n126\t### D5: Workflow Integration\n127\t\n128\tThe modified `/skill:measure` procedure becomes:\n129\t\n130\t1. Obtain SKILL.md file (existing Step 1)\n131\t2. Check prerequisites (existing Step 2)\n132\t3. Run baseline evaluation (existing Step 3)\n133\t4. Enhance the skill (existing Step 4)\n134\t5. **NEW: Parse enhancement diff** from Step 4's output\n135\t6. **NEW: Generate targeted cases** for uncovered enhanced patterns\n136\t7. **NEW: Interactive review** of generated cases\n137\t8. **NEW: Merge approved cases** into eval/cases/\n138\t9. Run re-evaluation against combined dataset (modified Step 5)\n139\t10. Compare results (existing Step 6)\n140\t11. **NEW: Report targeted case info** in summary (modified Step 7)\n141\t\n142\tSteps 5-8 are inserted between the existing Steps 4 and 5. They are skipped entirely when the enhancer reports \"already optimal\" (no diff to parse).\n143\t\n144\t### D6: eval.yaml Configuration\n145\t\n146\tAdd a `targeted_cases_per_pattern` field to the eval.yaml schema:\n147\t\n148\t```yaml\n149\t# Existing fields...\n150\tdataset:\n151\t  path: eval/cases\n152\t  targeted_cases_per_pattern: 1  # NEW: default 1, max 2\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\tThis field controls how many test cases are generated per enhanced pattern. Default is 1 if the field is absent.\n156\t\n157\t### D7: Partial Failure Handling\n158\t\n159\tIf targeted case generation fails for some patterns:\n160\t- Successfully generated cases are kept\n161\t- Failed patterns are listed in the review prompt with a warning\n162\t- The user can still proceed with the successfully generated cases\n163\t- The final summary reports both successful and failed targeted case counts\n164\t\n165\t## Complexity Tracking\n166\t\n167\tNo constitution violations to justify. The feature adds 5 new steps to an existing 7-step skill and one new config field. No new files, no new abstractions.\n168\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dac3d80-63df-4a77-86e1-2e7e2781a8a5","uuid":"3fa57a0b-0ef2-403b-a7ac-1ddfbe468907","timestamp":"2026-06-01T15:29:40.109Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/rhuss/Development/context-engineering/cc-skill/specs/004-targeted-eval-dataset/plan.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Targeted Eval Dataset for Enhancement Coverage\n\n**Branch**: `004-targeted-eval-dataset` | **Date**: 2026-05-31 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)\n**Input**: Feature specification from `specs/004-targeted-eval-dataset/spec.md`\n\n## Summary\n\nExtend `/skill:measure` to analyze the enhancement diff (the \"What Changed\" table from `/skill:enhance`), generate targeted test cases for enhanced patterns not already covered by the existing dataset, present them for interactive review, merge approved cases into `eval/cases/`, and run both baseline and enhanced evals against the combined dataset. This ensures the comparison reflects actual improvement in enhanced areas rather than only measuring pre-existing coverage.\n\n## Technical Context\n\n**Language/Version**: Bash (scripts), Markdown (SKILL.md skill definitions)\n**Primary Dependencies**: agent-eval-harness plugin (`/eval-run`, `/eval-dataset`), yq (YAML parsing), skill plugin (`/skill:enhance`, `/skill:check`)\n**Storage**: File-based eval case directories (`eval/cases/`)\n**Testing**: Manual testing against real SKILL.md files with eval infrastructure\n**Target Platform**: macOS/Linux (Claude Code environments)\n**Project Type**: Claude Code plugin (skill modification + supporting logic)\n**Performance Goals**: Targeted case generation adds no more than 30 seconds to the `/skill:measure` workflow (SC-003)\n**Constraints**: No nested `claude -p` sessions; all invocations within current session; must not modify existing test cases (FR-007)\n**Scale/Scope**: 1-2 targeted cases per enhanced pattern; bounded by `targeted_cases_per_pattern` in `eval.yaml`\n\n## Constitution Check\n\n*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*\n\nConstitution is a blank template. No gates to evaluate. Passes by default.\n\n## Project Structure\n\n### Documentation (this feature)\n\n```text\nspecs/004-targeted-eval-dataset/\n├── spec.md              # Feature specification\n├── plan.md              # This file\n├── research.md          # Phase 0: enhancement diff format, eval-dataset integration\n├── data-model.md        # Phase 1: entity definitions\n└── tasks.md             # Phase 2 output (created by /speckit-tasks)\n```\n\n### Source Code (repository root)\n\n```text\nskill/\n├── skills/\n│   └── measure/\n│       └── SKILL.md           # MODIFIED: add targeted case generation steps\n└── scripts/\n    └── compare-runs.sh        # Existing (no changes needed)\n\neval.yaml                      # MODIFIED: add targeted_cases_per_pattern config\n```\n\n**Structure Decision**: This feature modifies one existing file (`skill/skills/measure/SKILL.md`) and one config file (`eval.yaml`). No new files or directories are created in the source tree. The targeted case generation logic is embedded in the skill's procedure steps, not extracted into a separate script, because the generation relies on LLM capabilities (understanding which patterns were enhanced and what test inputs would exercise them).\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### D1: Enhancement Diff Capture\n\nThe enhancement diff is captured by parsing the \"What Changed\" markdown table that `/skill:enhance` outputs in Step 9c. This table has the structure:\n\n```markdown\n| Pattern Applied | What was added/changed | Why |\n|----------------|----------------------|-----|\n| Known Gotchas  | Added specific YAML validation pitfall | Domain has non-obvious failure modes |\n```\n\nAfter `/skill:enhance` completes (and the user applies changes), `/skill:measure` parses this table from the conversation output to extract:\n- Pattern names from the \"Pattern Applied\" column\n- Change descriptions from the \"What was added/changed\" column\n\nThis is the same approach used for detecting \"already optimal\" (reading conversation output for signals). No structured data file is needed because the table is well-formatted and parseable.\n\n**Edge case**: If the table is absent (user applied changes manually or output was truncated), treat as \"unknown diff\" and fall back to existing dataset only with a warning.\n\n### D2: Targeted Case Generation\n\nFor each pattern in the enhancement diff, `/skill:measure` generates targeted test cases by:\n\n1. Checking if an existing case in `eval/cases/` already targets this pattern (name-based matching on directory names and `annotations.yaml` content)\n2. If not covered, invoking `/eval-dataset` with a hint about which pattern to target\n3. Each generated case follows the existing case directory structure:\n   ```\n   eval/cases/case-NNN-targeted-<pattern-slug>/\n   ├── input.yaml         # skill_path pointing to a synthetic SKILL.md\n   ├── target-skill/\n   │   └── SKILL.md       # Synthetic skill designed to exercise the pattern\n   └── annotations.yaml   # Expected outcomes with targets_pattern metadata\n   ```\n\nThe `annotations.yaml` includes a `targets_pattern` field for traceability:\n```yaml\ndescription: \"Tests gotcha handling added by enhancement\"\ntargets_pattern: \"Known Gotchas\"\n```\n\n### D3: Deduplication Strategy\n\nBefore generating a case for an enhanced pattern, check existing cases:\n\n1. Scan all directories in `eval/cases/` for `annotations.yaml` files\n2. Check if any existing annotation has a `targets_pattern` field matching the pattern name\n3. Also check if the directory name contains the pattern slug (e.g., `case-*-known-gotchas`)\n4. Skip generation for patterns already covered\n\nThis is intentionally simple (string matching, not semantic analysis) to keep the workflow fast and deterministic.\n\n### D4: Interactive Review Flow\n\nAfter generating targeted cases (and before any eval run), `/skill:measure` presents a review prompt:\n\n1. Display a summary table of generated cases:\n   ```\n   | # | Case Directory | Targets Pattern | Input Synopsis |\n   |---|----------------|----------------|----------------|\n   | 1 | case-006-targeted-known-gotchas | Known Gotchas | YAML validation skill missing pitfall coverage |\n   ```\n\n2. Prompt: \"Proceed with eval? (y/n/edit)\"\n   - **y**: Continue with all generated cases\n   - **n**: Abort, remove generated cases, run with original dataset only\n   - **edit**: User modifies cases on disk, then confirms to continue\n\n3. If partial generation failure occurred, the summary includes a warning row for each failed pattern\n\n### D5: Workflow Integration\n\nThe modified `/skill:measure` procedure becomes:\n\n1. Obtain SKILL.md file (existing Step 1)\n2. Check prerequisites (existing Step 2)\n3. Run baseline evaluation (existing Step 3)\n4. Enhance the skill (existing Step 4)\n5. **NEW: Parse enhancement diff** from Step 4's output\n6. **NEW: Generate targeted cases** for uncovered enhanced patterns\n7. **NEW: Interactive review** of generated cases\n8. **NEW: Merge approved cases** into eval/cases/\n9. Run re-evaluation against combined dataset (modified Step 5)\n10. Compare results (existing Step 6)\n11. **NEW: Report targeted case info** in summary (modified Step 7)\n\nSteps 5-8 are inserted between the existing Steps 4 and 5. They are skipped entirely when the enhancer reports \"already optimal\" (no diff to parse).\n\n### D6: eval.yaml Configuration\n\nAdd a `targeted_cases_per_pattern` field to the eval.yaml schema:\n\n```yaml\n# Existing fields...\ndataset:\n  path: eval/cases\n  targeted_cases_per_pattern: 1  # NEW: default 1, max 2\n```\n\nThis field controls how many test cases are generated per enhanced pattern. Default is 1 if the field is absent.\n\n### D7: Partial Failure Handling\n\nIf targeted case generation fails for some patterns:\n- Successfully generated cases are kept\n- Failed patterns are listed in the review prompt with a warning\n- The user can still proceed with the successfully generated cases\n- The final summary reports both successful and failed targeted case counts\n\n## Complexity Tracking\n\nNo constitution violations to justify. The feature adds 5 new steps to an existing 7-step skill and one new config field. No new files, no new abstractions.\n","numLines":168,"startLine":1,"totalLines":168}}}
